    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## Change: consolidated duplicate detection into a single `identityKey`\n\nThe old code had three independent 409 checks \u2014 telephone, email, and last-name+address household. I replaced them with one derived key and rejection rule.\n\n**`identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`**, and a create is rejected with 409 only when a new owner's *whole* key equals an existing owner's.\n\n### Files changed\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n  - `addOwner` flow now normalizes telephone + email, resolves the new owner's `householdId`, then runs a single `rejectDuplicateIdentity(...)` in place of the three old checks.\n  - Added `rejectDuplicateIdentity`, plus `identityKey(...)` / `existingIdentityKey(...)` / `orEmpty(...)` helpers. Existing owners' keys are derived the same way (telephone re-normalized to E.164, email lower-cased) so formatting-only differences still collide.\n  - Split the household logic: new `resolveHouseholdId(...)` (pure, no mutation) feeds both the identity check and `assignHousehold`; `householdMembers(...)` extracted. Because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household with different telephones now get different keys and are both allowed.\n  - Removed `rejectDuplicateTelephone`, `rejectDuplicateEmail`, `rejectDuplicateHousehold`.\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `identityKey` string to the `Owner` schema (so `OwnerDto` exposes it).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 maps `identityKey` at read time from the stored telephone/email/householdId.\n- **`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException.java`** (new) + **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 one 409 handler naming `identityKey`; removed the three old exception classes and their handlers.\n\n### Verification\n- `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsIdentityCollision` (two owners sharing a telephone \u2192 409) passes.\n- Full offline `compile` and `test` builds succeed; no stale references to the removed types remain.\n\nOne behavioral note worth surfacing: because a duplicate now requires the *whole* key to match, two owners with the same telephone but different emails (or different households) are no longer rejected \u2014 that's the intended consequence of the spec (\"This changes existing behaviour\").",
